# Q: does a zone breed what it says it will, at the cadence it says, and does anything anywhere
# Q: shoot at a wall nothing can happen to?
#
#   MiVic.Game.exe --generator-demo --probe tools/probe/generator.probe --probe-out artifacts/probe/generator.txt
#
# The fixture: a derelict factory on the undeclared fourth team — hostile to every side, ignored by
# the victory rule, played by nobody — set to emit a Φύλακας every five seconds until it has given
# six, with a player's tank standing eighty metres south of it to be shot at. See ROADMAP §9 and
# the fixture's own comment for why the zone belongs to nobody.
#
# What to read:
#
#   - `zone` on the factory's own reading is the cadence witness: how many the zone has given and
#     when the next one is due. The census answers "how many are alive", which the fighting keeps
#     changing — the tank south of the zone kills wardens as they arrive — and `zone` answers "how
#     many has the zone emitted", which only the cadence moves. Ticks are what the clock is, so
#     "every five seconds" is exact, and after the sixth the count stops: a count is how many it
#     will *ever* emit, and a zone that has given everything it had is a place with a history.
#   - `order 508 attack 509` is the targeting half of "cannot be killed": the order is taken —
#     hostility and invulnerability are different questions and the factory IS at war with
#     everybody — and the tank drops it on the first tick, because acquisition may never hold a
#     target nothing can hurt. The damage half is pinned in the core tests, where a blast on the
#     factory's own square moves no health; no shipped ability is reachable at the tier a fixture
#     runs at, so the transcript asks the question the client can answer.
#   - the factory's slot is the fixture's own: the Clear below it takes the pool's tail, so the
#     factory lands on 509 for this fixture at this capacity, and the probe says so rather than
#     pretending the number is portable.

# --- the zone, before it has given anything -------------------------------------------------------
unit 509

# --- first emission: exact on the tick, not a frame either side -----------------------------------
tick 100
unit 509
tick 1
unit 509

# --- three more cadences, the tank south of the zone shooting the wardens while they land ---------
tick 300
unit 509

# --- the targeting half: an order taken, and dropped by the next tick -----------------------------
order 508 attack 509
tick 1
unit 508

# --- the spent zone: after the sixth, the clock stops for good ------------------------------------
tick 400
unit 509
tick 200
unit 509
count Warden
